WEBVTT

00:00:02.160 --> 00:00:07.450
The pain of being alone,
and the loneliness of everything being different...

00:00:07.450 --> 00:00:10.110
I’m sure everyone knows these things.

00:00:11.240 --> 00:00:16.480
Because there was somebody important to me, who shared things with me and supported me,

00:00:17.320 --> 00:00:19.380
I am here now.

00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:25.290
But without the power of magic, without fighting,

00:00:25.290 --> 00:00:28.180
what can I do?

00:00:28.180 --> 00:00:33.550
How should I answer those small eyes with nowhere to go?

00:00:35.340 --> 00:00:39.930
Magical Girl Lyrical Nanoha StrikerS<i>
will now begin.</i>

00:03:33.100 --> 00:03:34.980
Okay, everybody come here.

00:03:35.940 --> 00:03:37.760
Morning practice is done for the day.

00:03:37.760 --> 00:03:38.480
Yes, ma’am!

00:03:38.480 --> 00:03:42.060
There were no major problems today...
everything’s looking good.

00:03:42.060 --> 00:03:44.160
Keep at it!

00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:46.580
Thank you, ma’am!

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:50.330
I guess we’ve finally gotten used to our secondary modes.

00:03:50.330 --> 00:03:51.540
Yeah.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:58.120
It’s not a major change for Caro and I,
but it must be hard for Tia and Erio.

00:03:58.120 --> 00:04:00.720
The whole body’s changed.

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:02.790
To me it’s nothing.

00:04:02.790 --> 00:04:05.680
Dagger Mode is just a backup.

00:04:06.130 --> 00:04:07.600
Yes.

00:04:07.600 --> 00:04:10.170
It’s Erio’s that’s complicated.

00:04:10.170 --> 00:04:13.770
Strada’s secondary is pretty crazy.

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:15.580
You think?

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:19.760
I think it’s cool, Strada.

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:21.880
Thanks, m’lady.

00:04:21.880 --> 00:04:24.690
I’ll continue to train with Strada.

00:04:24.690 --> 00:04:26.280
I’ll do my best!

00:04:33.410 --> 00:04:34.740
Vivio!

00:04:40.900 --> 00:04:42.700
Morning, Vivio.

00:04:42.700 --> 00:04:44.620
Did you get yourself up today?

00:04:44.620 --> 00:04:45.880
Yep!

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:47.500
Good morning, Fate.

00:04:47.500 --> 00:04:49.390
Good morning, Nanoha.

00:04:49.390 --> 00:04:53.590
Vivio, say good morning to Nanoha.

00:04:53.590 --> 00:04:57.230
Good morning.

00:04:57.230 --> 00:05:00.340
You can eat breakfast with us, right?

00:05:00.340 --> 00:05:00.780
Yeah.

00:05:00.780 --> 00:05:02.740
Breakfast?

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:04.130
That’s right.

00:05:04.130 --> 00:05:05.530
Come on, let’s go.

00:05:06.320 --> 00:05:08.950
What’s on the menu today, I wonder?

00:05:10.990 --> 00:05:16.040
Attention all operatives: would P.F.C. Lanster please report to the commander’s office?

00:05:17.580 --> 00:05:22.130
You see, I’m heading to the Main Office today,

00:05:22.130 --> 00:05:26.130
and I wanted to know if you’d come with me, Teana.

00:05:27.070 --> 00:05:28.010
I see.

00:05:28.010 --> 00:05:31.130
The person we’re meeting today is Captain Fate’s brother,

00:05:31.130 --> 00:05:33.930
Admiral Chrono Harlaown.

00:05:33.930 --> 00:05:34.870
I see.

00:05:34.870 --> 00:05:37.980
He’s a ship’s captain and an Enforcer.

00:05:37.980 --> 00:05:44.440
I thought it’d be good for your future if you had some experience meeting important people like that.

00:05:44.440 --> 00:05:46.520
Thank you, ma’am!

00:05:46.520 --> 00:05:48.360
I’d be honored to go with you!

00:05:50.410 --> 00:05:51.940
Oh, where’s Teana?

00:05:51.940 --> 00:05:54.320
She seems to be accompanying Commander Yagami

00:05:54.320 --> 00:05:56.070
to the Main Office or something.

00:05:56.070 --> 00:05:56.790
I see.

00:05:56.790 --> 00:05:59.790
Are you staying in the office today, Nanoha?

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:00.710
That’s right.

00:06:01.500 --> 00:06:06.170
Lightning is out investigating today,
and the lieutenants are off.

00:06:06.170 --> 00:06:09.660
You and I are the only
front-line troops here today, Subaru.

00:06:10.380 --> 00:06:13.140
I’ll pray nothing happens.

00:06:13.140 --> 00:06:17.060
By the way, what’s Vivio doing during the day?

00:06:17.880 --> 00:06:19.980
She’s staying in her room.

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:26.150
The housekeeper, Aina, is looking after her,
and Zafira is on guard.

00:06:26.150 --> 00:06:26.800
Did I do it?

00:06:28.640 --> 00:06:29.610
I did it!

00:06:29.610 --> 00:06:32.070
Oh, that’s great, sweetie!

00:06:32.070 --> 00:06:33.030
Thanks!

00:06:38.440 --> 00:06:41.860
Anchor placement location secured.

00:06:41.860 --> 00:06:43.340
Initiating standby status.

00:06:44.130 --> 00:06:45.760
Begin resupply and inspection.

00:06:45.760 --> 00:06:48.340
Everyone who’s free, go and get some rest!

00:06:48.340 --> 00:06:49.260
Sir!

00:06:49.260 --> 00:06:50.780
Good work, Chrono.

00:06:53.180 --> 00:06:56.470
We still have some time until Hayate gets here.

00:06:56.470 --> 00:06:59.100
Well, let’s just relax and wait.

00:06:59.100 --> 00:07:00.830
Oh, right.

00:07:02.550 --> 00:07:04.020
Want some cake?

00:07:04.020 --> 00:07:07.080
It’s homemade, but it’s pretty good.

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:10.730
I told you I don’t like sweet things.

00:07:10.730 --> 00:07:12.850
It’s not too sweet.

00:07:12.850 --> 00:07:14.760
I guess I’ll have some.

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:15.480
Great!

00:07:15.480 --> 00:07:20.610
Anyway, just like you asked, I secretly looked into the internal situation at Surface HQ,

00:07:20.610 --> 00:07:23.080
especially the people around Lt. General Gaiz.

00:07:23.880 --> 00:07:28.800
He’s quite the character, an amazing strong-arm politician.

00:07:28.800 --> 00:07:32.840
He’s a powerful force and has an air of authority that draws people to him.

00:07:32.840 --> 00:07:35.760
I’ll admit he’s impressive.

00:07:35.760 --> 00:07:39.210
The head of administration is his subordinate as well.

00:07:39.210 --> 00:07:45.640
Even though there’s no end to the bad rumors about him,
he <i>is</i> the guardian of order on the surface.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:48.470
And he’s well-supported by various corporations and political groups,

00:07:48.470 --> 00:07:51.950
plus he’s in good standing with the Bureau High Council.

00:07:51.950 --> 00:07:57.910
He’s definitely somebody who’s hard for the Main Office to deal with.

00:07:57.910 --> 00:07:59.110
Yes.

00:07:59.110 --> 00:08:03.280
We can’t intervene carelessly, with relations between the ground and naval forces being as they are,

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:07.380
and with relations between Surface HQ
and the Main Office, conflict with every single thing—

00:08:08.330 --> 00:08:10.760
Excuse me, Captain Chrono.

00:08:11.300 --> 00:08:14.260
Lt. Colonel Hayate Yagami is here.

00:08:19.720 --> 00:08:20.640
Hayate.

00:08:20.640 --> 00:08:23.020
Welcome to the <i>Claudia.</i>

00:08:23.020 --> 00:08:26.970
It’s quite the ship. Just as I imagined one of the latest ships would be like...

00:08:26.970 --> 00:08:27.820
I guess.

00:08:27.820 --> 00:08:30.270
I heard you underwent a special inspection.

00:08:30.270 --> 00:08:31.780
Did it go well?

00:08:31.780 --> 00:08:34.870
Yes, we managed to avoid an immediate hearing.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:35.820
Oh, right.

00:08:35.820 --> 00:08:40.440
I’ll introduce you. This is the leader of
the forwards... she wants to become an Enforcer.

00:08:40.440 --> 00:08:43.710
Private First Class Teana Lanster.

00:08:43.710 --> 00:08:44.780
Hello.

00:08:44.780 --> 00:08:46.130
Nice to meetcha.

00:08:49.990 --> 00:08:51.510
Thanks.

00:08:51.510 --> 00:08:53.400
Oh, have a seat.

00:08:53.400 --> 00:08:55.680
No, I’ll stand here.

00:08:56.800 --> 00:08:59.600
You told the front-line troops everything?

00:09:01.590 --> 00:09:03.300
You want some too, right?

00:09:03.300 --> 00:09:05.560
No, I’m fine.

00:09:05.560 --> 00:09:07.730
I see.

00:09:10.150 --> 00:09:13.610
A terrorist attack on Surface HQ?

00:09:13.610 --> 00:09:17.700
It’s possible, that’s all.

00:09:17.700 --> 00:09:19.580
But if you think about it,

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:24.880
The magic defenses at HQ facilities are impressive,
but if they use the Gadgets...

00:09:24.880 --> 00:09:25.570
Yes.

00:09:25.570 --> 00:09:31.700
The Bureau generally forbids the use of mass-based weapons, so it would be hard to deal with them.

00:09:31.700 --> 00:09:33.420
Mass-based weapons?

00:09:34.520 --> 00:09:39.600
I guess you could say they’re
physical weapons that don’t use magic, maybe.

00:09:40.760 --> 00:09:45.270
They fire physical matter that strikes the enemy or explodes.

00:09:45.270 --> 00:09:49.650
Historically, Midchilda made heavy use of
those weapons during wartime, as did Ancient Belka.

00:09:49.650 --> 00:09:55.820
I’ve heard of them. Once they’re made,
even a kid can use them,

00:09:55.820 --> 00:09:59.990
and that moving a finger could destroy a town or an entire world.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:01.110
Yes.

00:10:01.110 --> 00:10:05.440
Ever since its founding, the Bureau
has rooted out those weapons

00:10:05.440 --> 00:10:10.580
and started to regulate the use of Lost Logia
for peace and safety.

00:10:10.580 --> 00:10:13.380
That was about 150 years ago.

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:16.310
But weapons are needed for a variety of reasons.

00:10:16.310 --> 00:10:18.300
Now then, what did we do?

00:10:20.170 --> 00:10:25.960
Being both relatively clean and safe, we encouraged society towards magic.

00:10:27.270 --> 00:10:28.590
That’s right.

00:10:28.590 --> 00:10:35.820
The Bureau’s effective use of magic is what enabled it to manage the various worlds.

00:10:35.820 --> 00:10:39.910
They established their Main Office
in the Dimensional Sea where all the worlds float,

00:10:39.910 --> 00:10:44.320
and on their homeworld, Midchilda, they built Surface HQ.

00:10:44.320 --> 00:10:48.800
Oh! That was the beginning of the New Calendar, 75 years ago.

00:10:48.800 --> 00:10:49.570
Yes.

00:10:49.570 --> 00:10:54.580
And who was it that saw the Bureau through the beginning of the New Calendar,

00:10:54.580 --> 00:10:57.820
when things were most chaotic,
and brought peace to the worlds?

00:10:57.820 --> 00:11:00.130
The renowned Three Admirals.

00:11:01.460 --> 00:11:02.710
I see.

00:11:02.710 --> 00:11:06.340
But let’s put worlds history aside for now...

00:11:06.340 --> 00:11:08.100
I’m sorry.

00:11:08.100 --> 00:11:11.770
What I’m saying here is that if it looks like the Gadgets are going to appear,

00:11:11.770 --> 00:11:14.680
Riot Force 6 will go into action
even if it has nothing to do with the Relics.

00:11:14.680 --> 00:11:16.280
Do your best, okay?

00:11:16.280 --> 00:11:17.360
Yes, ma’am!

00:11:17.360 --> 00:11:21.780
We’ve gotten pretty used to fighting Gadgets... it’ll be okay.

00:11:28.950 --> 00:11:32.500
Yes, it’s true that the information comes from an unreliable source,

00:11:32.500 --> 00:11:37.450
but everyone says the notion that
the Bureau might be destroyed is absurd.

00:11:37.450 --> 00:11:41.380
Even if Surface HQ did fall to terrorism or a <i>coup d’etat,</i>

00:11:41.380 --> 00:11:47.010
nobody’s willing to believe that
the Main Office could be taken down with it.

00:11:47.010 --> 00:11:50.840
Well, the Main Office <i>is</i> enhancing its defenses.

00:11:50.840 --> 00:11:53.090
The problem is Surface HQ.

00:11:53.090 --> 00:11:56.720
Lt. General Gaiz refuses to believe the prophecy.

00:11:56.720 --> 00:11:59.100
He’s not taking any special precautions.

00:11:59.100 --> 00:12:03.070
It’s difficult for different organizations to cooperate.

00:12:03.070 --> 00:12:10.620
If “cooperation” is recast as “interfering with our internal affairs” or “meddling”, then it becomes a matter of dispute.

00:12:10.620 --> 00:12:16.540
And even without that, the military power and influence Surface HQ has on Mid has been considered a problem.

00:12:16.540 --> 00:12:20.510
Therefore, you couldn’t offer any major help that would be noticed in terms of military forces.

00:12:20.510 --> 00:12:22.210
I’m sorry.

00:12:22.210 --> 00:12:26.390
I’d like to keep political problems away from the front lines.

00:12:26.390 --> 00:12:30.800
Even if it’s cheating, you would need a force
that could act freely on the surface.

00:12:30.800 --> 00:12:33.800
If it all that happens is we have a Relic Incident, that’s fine.

00:12:33.800 --> 00:12:39.650
And if things get worse, we’d need somebody who could watch the situation up close...

00:12:39.650 --> 00:12:42.390
And until Surface HQ starts to take things seriously

00:12:42.390 --> 00:12:46.870
or the Bureau and the Church
send their own forces in to keep things stable.

00:12:46.870 --> 00:12:49.280
That’s what Riot Force 6 is for.

00:12:52.250 --> 00:12:56.750
Of course, we won’t cause
any trouble for you outside your missions.

00:12:56.750 --> 00:12:58.930
Don’t worry about it.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:03.620
We’ve received a firm promise from
Lt. Colonel Yagami that she’ll take care of her staff.

00:13:03.620 --> 00:13:04.880
Yes.

00:13:04.880 --> 00:13:11.680
Once again, as a knight with the Church of
the Holy King’s Church Knights, I, Carim Gracia, ask you.

00:13:11.680 --> 00:13:16.120
It will be an inglorious and dangerous mission,

00:13:16.120 --> 00:13:19.770
but will you help us?

00:13:19.770 --> 00:13:23.350
We can’t do much, but we’ll do all we can.

00:13:23.350 --> 00:13:25.240
We accept.

00:13:25.240 --> 00:13:29.160
The safety and peace of the land and sea...

00:13:29.160 --> 00:13:33.580
The future and security of everyone in the unit, including these children...

00:13:33.580 --> 00:13:35.430
Hayate’s position...

00:13:35.430 --> 00:13:37.210
And the sky where Nanoha flies...

00:13:37.210 --> 00:13:39.700
It’ll be hard to protect them all,

00:13:39.700 --> 00:13:41.570
but I will do my best.

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:45.460
Lend me a hand, Bardiche.

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:02.860
Okay!

00:14:12.490 --> 00:14:13.900
Nanoha?

00:14:13.900 --> 00:14:16.180
Hey, Nanoha?

00:14:16.180 --> 00:14:17.780
Huh... wha... sorry.

00:14:17.780 --> 00:14:18.700
What?

00:14:18.700 --> 00:14:22.300
Nothing really, I just wanted to let you know
that you finished the data set.

00:14:22.300 --> 00:14:23.960
Oh... you’re right.

00:14:26.130 --> 00:14:28.210
I need to pay attention.

00:14:28.210 --> 00:14:29.340
Not at all.

00:14:31.710 --> 00:14:33.240
It’s lunch time.

00:14:33.590 --> 00:14:37.980
I’m going back to the dorms and eating with Vivio.
Would you come with me, Subaru?

00:14:37.980 --> 00:14:38.800
Yes.

00:14:38.800 --> 00:14:40.140
I’ll go with you.

00:14:42.560 --> 00:14:46.680
But what’s going to happen to Vivio now?

00:14:46.680 --> 00:14:51.550
If we find a family who’ll accept her, that’d be the best.

00:14:52.240 --> 00:14:54.310
That’s hard.

00:14:54.310 --> 00:14:56.820
She’s not normal, after all.

00:14:56.820 --> 00:14:58.410
That’s true.

00:15:01.830 --> 00:15:05.200
I think it’ll take time to find one.

00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:09.440
So, for now, I think it would be best if I looked after her.

00:15:10.010 --> 00:15:16.050
I’m thinking of being her guardian, like Captain Fate is to Erio and Caro.

00:15:16.050 --> 00:15:17.340
That’s a great idea!

00:15:17.340 --> 00:15:18.970
I’m sure Vivio will be happy.

00:15:20.000 --> 00:15:21.160
Happy, huh?

00:15:21.160 --> 00:15:22.940
Definitely!

00:15:26.530 --> 00:15:27.720
See?

00:15:27.720 --> 00:15:29.600
She doesn’t really understand.

00:15:29.600 --> 00:15:31.950
What should we say so that she understands?

00:15:33.910 --> 00:15:38.360
So, for a while, Nanoha will be your mom, Vivio.

00:15:38.360 --> 00:15:39.920
Mama?

00:15:44.250 --> 00:15:46.130
You can call me that if you want.

00:15:49.410 --> 00:15:53.760
Until we find your real mother, Vivio,
I’ll be your mama for a little while.

00:15:53.760 --> 00:15:55.680
Is that okay with you, Vivio?

00:15:59.300 --> 00:16:01.480
Mama.

00:16:01.480 --> 00:16:03.390
Yes, Vivio?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:10.980
Why are you crying?

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:12.900
It’s okay, Vivio.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:25.740
By the way, what about the <i>Arthra?</i>

00:16:25.740 --> 00:16:28.090
It’s going to be dismantled next month.

00:16:28.090 --> 00:16:29.090
I see.

00:16:29.090 --> 00:16:32.920
It seemed like it could still run
for a while longer last I saw it.

00:16:32.920 --> 00:16:35.760
We don’t think it could last through a long mission.

00:16:35.760 --> 00:16:41.320
That’s sad. The <i>Arthra</i> holds a lot of memories for us.

00:16:41.320 --> 00:16:43.230
It’s worked hard for a long time.

00:16:43.230 --> 00:16:46.150
We need to let it rest.

00:16:46.150 --> 00:16:48.320
Here’s your data.

00:16:48.320 --> 00:16:50.610
It’s important data, so be careful.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:51.670
Yes.

00:16:54.560 --> 00:16:55.780
Teana, was it?

00:16:55.780 --> 00:16:56.810
Y-Yes.

00:16:56.810 --> 00:16:59.410
What do you think of Hayate?

00:16:59.410 --> 00:17:00.730
Well,

00:17:00.730 --> 00:17:03.700
I think she’s an impressive mage and a talented commander.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:05.620
I see.

00:17:05.620 --> 00:17:09.830
Hayate, Chrono, and my stepsister Carim.

00:17:09.830 --> 00:17:13.200
The three of them have been friends for a long time,

00:17:13.200 --> 00:17:16.220
and thanks to that, they get along with me.

00:17:16.220 --> 00:17:17.210
Yes.

00:17:17.210 --> 00:17:18.550
I know that.

00:17:18.550 --> 00:17:24.060
She’s another user of Ancient Belkan magic, but more than that, Hayate is a good girl.

00:17:24.550 --> 00:17:26.040
She’s a sweetheart.

00:17:26.040 --> 00:17:27.480
Yes.

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:30.400
I think of her like a little sister.

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:32.980
So I’m kind of worried about her.

00:17:32.980 --> 00:17:33.820
I see.

00:17:33.820 --> 00:17:40.200
Rare Skills and powerful magic, strong power, and the authority to have other people serve her...

00:17:40.200 --> 00:17:45.700
Having that power also implies a degree of isolation.

00:17:45.700 --> 00:17:47.410
That’s what I think.

00:17:47.410 --> 00:17:48.500
I see.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:51.240
Of course, she’ll be needed.

00:17:51.240 --> 00:17:52.480
She’ll be relied on.

00:17:52.480 --> 00:17:59.380
But not as a person.
It’ll be the power she possesses being relied on.

00:17:59.380 --> 00:18:02.460
Of course, that’s an extreme case.

00:18:02.460 --> 00:18:05.140
It’s not actually like that.

00:18:05.140 --> 00:18:06.590
Yes, I understand.

00:18:06.590 --> 00:18:11.850
“With great power comes great pressure
and loneliness,” is what you’re saying.

00:18:11.850 --> 00:18:13.130
Yes, that’s right.

00:18:14.100 --> 00:18:17.570
Anyway, so what I’m trying to say is, well...

00:18:17.570 --> 00:18:23.020
I’m sure that a lot of things may happen between a commander and her front-line troops.

00:18:23.020 --> 00:18:30.540
But I’d like you to treat her not just as a superior,
but as a person—as another girl.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:34.290
Not just Hayate, but your captains too.

00:18:34.950 --> 00:18:36.620
Roger.

00:18:36.620 --> 00:18:40.180
We front-line troops will do the best we can.

00:18:45.680 --> 00:18:47.980
I took another look at the squad data,

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:51.090
but Hayate is truly blessed to have family and staff like that.

00:18:51.090 --> 00:18:51.840
Agreed.

00:18:51.840 --> 00:18:53.680
Teana’s a good kid,

00:18:53.680 --> 00:18:58.020
but I’m sure her guilt isn’t going to go away that easily.

00:18:58.020 --> 00:19:01.110
I think Hayate is trying too hard, as always.

00:19:01.110 --> 00:19:06.070
If she can make it through this incident,
that will be proof of her suitability as a commander.

00:19:06.070 --> 00:19:09.870
And there will be less that people can say about the Book of Darkness Incident.

00:19:11.080 --> 00:19:15.030
Even if Nanoha and Fate are with her, I’m worried.

00:19:15.030 --> 00:19:17.410
I’d like to help her.

00:19:17.410 --> 00:19:21.510
The Main Office can’t act openly, as you just said.

00:19:22.210 --> 00:19:23.830
Leave it to me.

00:19:23.830 --> 00:19:27.430
The position of Inspector is suited to covert actions.

00:19:27.430 --> 00:19:29.850
Thanks, I’m counting on you.

00:19:29.850 --> 00:19:32.430
Teana, you haven’t eaten yet, right?

00:19:32.430 --> 00:19:34.480
Want to stop somewhere and get a bite?

00:19:34.480 --> 00:19:35.150
Yes.

00:19:35.150 --> 00:19:41.110
Commander Yagami, it’s a bit far,
but there’s a great restaurant up ahead.

00:19:41.110 --> 00:19:43.030
Really?

00:19:43.030 --> 00:19:46.230
Inspector Acous told me about it.

00:19:46.230 --> 00:19:47.450
Would you like to go?

00:19:47.450 --> 00:19:50.030
That sounds nice. Let’s go.

00:19:50.030 --> 00:19:51.840
Okay, I’ll show you the way.

00:19:51.840 --> 00:19:52.370
Great

00:19:52.370 --> 00:19:53.740
What kind of place is it?

00:19:53.740 --> 00:19:55.340
They say the fish there is great.

00:19:57.800 --> 00:20:03.470
We’ve received data once again from Riot Force 6
along with their inspection of the scene.

00:20:03.470 --> 00:20:08.060
With the template they’re using for their magic circles
and the signals from the power source they’re using,

00:20:08.060 --> 00:20:11.360
they’re at a far higher level than what we’ve run into before.

00:20:11.360 --> 00:20:13.310
I guess there’s no doubt, then.

00:20:13.310 --> 00:20:14.260
Yes.

00:20:14.260 --> 00:20:16.540
All of them are combat cyborgs

00:20:16.540 --> 00:20:19.230
created using the latest technology.

00:20:23.860 --> 00:20:28.790
I need to match Marie’s analyzed data with Riot Force 6’s.

00:20:28.790 --> 00:20:32.000
It’s not something we can do without meeting in person.

00:20:32.000 --> 00:20:33.750
I guess I’ll go.

00:20:33.750 --> 00:20:35.110
Yes.

00:20:35.110 --> 00:20:39.030
Commander Yagami seems like she will return after 0800.

00:20:39.030 --> 00:20:41.420
Are you busy, Chief Engineer Mariel?

00:20:41.420 --> 00:20:43.620
I’ll go along.

00:20:43.620 --> 00:20:46.090
I haven’t seen Subaru lately.

00:20:46.090 --> 00:20:47.790
Thanks.

00:20:47.790 --> 00:20:50.420
Okay, keep yourself busy until it’s time to go.

00:20:50.420 --> 00:20:51.020
Ginga.

00:20:51.020 --> 00:20:52.090
Yes, sir.

00:20:52.090 --> 00:20:53.720
Let’s go to the break room, Marie.

00:20:53.720 --> 00:20:54.690
Sure.

00:21:02.440 --> 00:21:06.320
I guess I should have expected it.

00:21:06.320 --> 00:21:10.700
Nothing’s finished yet.

00:21:10.700 --> 00:21:13.120
This is tough!

00:21:26.900 --> 00:21:29.890
I see. Nanoha’s your mom now.

00:21:29.890 --> 00:21:30.720
Yeah.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:35.140
And I’ll be your mom in a way too, Vivio.

00:21:36.600 --> 00:21:39.550
I’m your godmother.

00:21:39.550 --> 00:21:43.070
Vivio, it’s my job to watch over you and your Mama Nanoha.

00:21:45.490 --> 00:21:49.910
Mama Nanoha and Mama Fate?

00:21:49.910 --> 00:21:51.480
Yes.

00:21:51.480 --> 00:21:52.700
Right.

00:21:54.820 --> 00:21:55.790
Mama?

00:21:55.790 --> 00:21:57.250
Yes?

00:22:05.550 --> 00:22:09.380
Both Nanoha and Fate being her mom...

00:22:09.380 --> 00:22:12.220
Vivio is really invincible.

00:22:13.800 --> 00:22:18.650
But Fate’s your guardian, and Nanoha’s teaching you.

00:22:18.650 --> 00:22:21.800
Well, that’s true, but...

00:22:24.410 --> 00:22:29.530
By the way, how do you both think of Fate? As more like a mother or an older sister?

00:22:29.530 --> 00:22:33.450
I think of her as a kind older sister.

00:22:34.530 --> 00:22:36.400
It could go either way for me.

00:22:36.400 --> 00:22:37.870
It’s hard to decide.

00:22:37.870 --> 00:22:43.990
I wonder if Fate would rather have Erio as a kid or as a younger brother.

00:22:43.990 --> 00:22:45.650
Let’s ask her tomorrow.

00:22:46.340 --> 00:22:49.280
I’m sorry, Caro, but don’t do that!

00:22:53.430 --> 00:22:56.220
A mother, huh?

00:23:00.850 --> 00:23:04.820
What happened then isn’t over.

00:23:06.780 --> 00:23:10.720
The Combat Cyborg Incident that killed my mother.

00:25:17.360 --> 00:25:19.360
The investigation
gets closer to the truth.

00:25:19.360 --> 00:25:21.460
As mother and child,
and as sister and sister,

00:25:21.460 --> 00:25:23.340
we enjoy a time of peace.

00:25:23.340 --> 00:25:25.260
Along with everyone’s bonds with each other.

00:25:32.040 --> 00:25:34.270
Take off!
